# S-044: audio thread timing, driven by the fake clock. start_time is the clock value when the thread starts;
# tick k (1-based) is due at start + floor-ish(k*1024 * 1e9 / rate) computed from the absolute sample count (no drift
# accumulation); start_ts passed to the input callback is the previous due time (start_time for tick 1).
aclock 1000000000
aopen main 48000 FLOAT_PLANAR STEREO
atick 3
aclose
# a rate that does not divide 1e9 evenly: 44100
aclock 0
aopen main 44100 FLOAT_PLANAR STEREO
atick 4
aclose
# exact formula: (n / rate) * 1e9 + ((n % rate) * 1e9) / rate with n = 1024 * k
aclock 123456789012
aopen main 8000 FLOAT_PLANAR MONO
atick 2
aclose
aclock 0
aopen main 3 FLOAT_PLANAR MONO
atick 3
aclose
